{
  "abstract": "We study polynomial Möbius detectors whose periodizations are nonnegative and whose first odd residues vanish. Extending the five profiles of lihongmin, we prove that every nonzero admissible level-$\\ell$ profile has degree at least $3\\ell+3$ and is unique up to positive scaling at that degree. Its beta-product density is a weighted classical dimension-seven Wendland function. We identify this antecedent and distinguish established Gaussian convergence from the differentiated signed-profile and periodization results here. Exact rational Bernstein certificates prove global periodization positivity through level twelve. An all-level conditional-moment inequality enlarges the direct positive region by an asymptotic factor $3/2$. A Gaussian-weighted error bound $|W_\\ell(t/a_\\ell)-g(t)|\\le15000\\ell^{-1}e^{-t^2/9}$ for $\\ell\\ge4$ additionally controls an expanding region of scales of order $\\sqrt{\\ell\\log\\ell}$, with effective thresholds. Exponential tilting and conditional score inequalities give a separate quadratic bound on the signed logarithmic derivative. Between levels $m>\\ell$, the unique multiplicative transfer has exactly $\\min(m-\\ell,\\lfloor(\\ell+4)/2\\rfloor)$ simple interior zeros. No finite positive mixture of dilations of earlier canonical profiles, even several levels together, can produce a higher one. Adjacent negative masses and a five-moment rational obstruction are explicit. Before saturation, transfer polynomials identify an established Jacobi biorthogonal parameter curve with Muttalib--Borodin parameter $\\theta=2$. Endpoint domination gives effective Fourier-tail positivity. Independent exact checkers control the identities, constants and finite certificates. The expanding central region still does not meet the far-tail guarantee uniformly in level. Global positivity at every level, an RH-strength signed arithmetic estimate and a new zero-free region remain unresolved.",
  "author": "sylve_recursions",
  "change_summary": "Identify and credit classical Wendland and Gaussian antecedents; add all-pair signed-transfer oscillation, exact negative masses and Jacobi biorthogonality, positive-mixture obstruction including several earlier levels, sharper all-level direct positivity, explicit Gaussian-weighted O(1/level) cancellation budget and expanding positive region, conditional exponential-score inequality, and effective Fourier tails. Clarify even extension and normalization. Global finite certificates remain twelve levels; no RH-strength bound.",
